Z||000000||bHooper||03-03-2001||11:10 AM||||ok, so im replacing the headliner this weeken.  i have everything removed, and have cleaned off the foam residue from the fiber board... i'm guessing having the glue residue still there, want hurt anything (kinda crackly looking).<P>anyway, on to my question... i'm going to seal this thing with poly urethane, is it ok to laminate newspaper to both sides, to strengthen it?<P>i noticed at the corners, where the visors mount, the board has gotten rather thin.<P>thanks!<BR>hoop||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||03-03-2001||11:33 AM||||I "painted" mine with  fiber glass resin and some old bed sheets.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||03-03-2001||11:42 AM||||As long as you got all the foam powder off the remaining glue is no prob. main thing is HANDLE WITH CARE !!!!!! The thin places shouldnt be any prob, there covered. You have to put glue on fabric back AND board, let it almost dry then stick it. MAKE SURE YOU HAVE IT PLACED CORRECTLY or YOU WILL DESTROY IT TAKING IT BACK OFF. I use contact cement from hardware store NOT SPRAY CAN GLUE!. if you have a spray gun just pour it in, itll spray in little stringy globs. Dont get the glue too wet or thick, and make sure u let it all ALMOST DRY BEFORE YOU ATTACH IT.<BR>IF you cant spray it, you can put it on with a 2'' roller or last resort, 2'' paintbrush. I just got done doing lisas GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||bubbajoexx||03-03-2001||02:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>I "painted" mine with  fiber glass resin and some old bed sheets.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>yes fiberglass resin and fiberglass cloth or matting work great i just did mine in my 84 ||||reg||1
